WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.080
Image scanning examines packages and files in a container image and compares identified

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.460
components with vulnerability data.

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.080
Software composition analysis focuses on application libraries and transitive

00:00:12.300 --> 00:00:13.420
dependencies.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.240
Together they provide a starting inventory of possible exposure.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.980
Package inventories and SBOMs improve traceability.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:24.800
An SBOM records component names, versions, suppliers,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:27.420
and relationships in a standard form.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:32.280
It can be generated during the build and retained with the image so future vulnerability

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.580
intelligence can be evaluated without rebuilding solely for discovery.

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:41.840
Vulnerability databases map component identifiers and versions to published findings and

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:43.660
remediation information.

00:00:43.880 --> 00:00:48.600
Results depend on accurate package detection, distribution metadata, naming,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.500
and database freshness.

00:00:50.720 --> 00:00:55.520
Different tools may report different findings because their data and analysis differ.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:59.820
False positives occur when a scanner matches a component that is not affected,

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:03.960
has a backported fix, or is present but not used as assumed.

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:09.300
False negatives can result from incomplete inventories, unsupported package formats,

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:13.920
copied binaries, stale data, or components that the tool cannot identify.

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:19.420
A finding becomes operationally useful when it maps to an exact image digest and running

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:20.520
workload.

00:01:20.740 --> 00:01:24.420
Registries may contain old or development images that are not deployed,

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.960
while a cluster may still run a digest that no longer has a familiar tag.

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:34.540
Combine pipeline scans, registry scans, SBOM analysis, and runtime inventory.

00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:40.520
Preserve scanner version, database time, image identity, disposition, and evidence.

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:46.180
Scanning discovers candidates for triage; it does not replace ownership, risk analysis,

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.560
testing, or verification that remediation reached production.
